      <div class="worship-celestial" aria-hidden="true"><span class="worship-moon">☾</span><span class="worship-star worship-star-one">✦</span><span class="worship-star worship-star-two">✧</span><span class="worship-cloud worship-cloud-one"></span><span class="worship-cloud worship-cloud-two"></span></div>
      <header class="worship-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Read them carefully</p><p class="worship-constellation" aria-hidden="true">✦&nbsp;✧&nbsp;✦</p><h1>The <em>Rules.</em></h1></header>
      <div class="worship-prose rules-prose">
        <p>The moon never begs for attention. She just pulls the tide, and everything obeys.</p>
        <p>I keep three rules in my world. They are simple, they are complete, and they are not negotiable. Everything else on this site, every page, every dynamic, every privilege, is built on top of these three. Read them twice. Then read the addendum below, because the rules tell you how to behave, and the addendum tells you what you are.</p>
        <h2>Rule One: Be <em>Respectful.</em></h2>
        <p>You address me properly. Always. You remember I'm a person before you remember I'm a goddess, and somehow you manage to worship both.</p>
        <p>Respect means: you greet me like a woman worth impressing. You ask, you don't demand. You say thank you, and you mean it. You don't touch, not with words, not with assumptions, not with familiarity I haven't granted. My time is Mine. My attention is Mine. My body, my life, and my decisions are Mine, and respect means you never once behave as though any of it is owed to you.</p>
        <p>Respect also means honesty about who I am: I am not your girlfriend, I am not your fantasy puppet, and I am not a woman you get to manage or correct. I am the woman you applied to serve. Behave like it, consistently, and you'll find me the warmest goddess you've ever belonged to.</p>
        <p>Respect fails in small moments. The Sub who's charming in public and careless in private doesn't last here. Neither does the one who's generous on payday and forgetful the week after. I watch how you treat me when you're tired, when you're busy, when you're not getting anything out of it. That's the respect that counts, and it's the respect I keep.</p>
        <h2>Rule Two: Be <em>Generous.</em></h2>
        <p>I don't set minimums for my attention. I don't have to. The men who belong here already know what they're willing to give before I ask.</p>
        <p>Generosity is not about the number. It's about the posture. A tribute is you telling me what I'm worth to you, in the only language that never lies. Words are free. Everyone has beautiful words. The men in my world learned a long time ago that the truest sentence a Sub can write is the one attached to a tribute.</p>
        <p>I want to be precise about this, because precision matters: I already have money. I don't need yours. I want it. The difference is everything. A woman who needs your money performs for it. A woman who wants it receives it, and spends her energy on taking care of you instead. You are not paying for my life. My life was expensive before you arrived. You are contributing to a world you get to be a small, treasured part of. That's the privilege. Don't ever confuse it with a transaction.</p>
        <p>Generosity also means generosity of spirit. Effort. Attention. Follow-through. The man who tributes beautifully and then disappears until he wants something is not generous, he's a customer, and I don't keep customers. The man who remembers what I told him last month, who checks in when I'm traveling, who does the task I forgot I even assigned, that man is generous, and I keep him, and I keep him well.</p>
        <h2>Rule Three: Be <em>Honest.</em></h2>
        <p>About who you are, what you want, and where your lines are.</p>
        <p>I take limits seriously. I take you seriously. When you tell me where your lines are, they stay where you put them, full stop. That is not negotiable, and it is not a loophole for me or for you, and any man who wishes his limits were pushed without asking should be having a different conversation with himself before he ever fills out my intake.</p>
        <p>Honesty also means: no lying about your experience, your resources, or your intentions. No hiding a wife who doesn't know, only to have it surface later as an emergency. No pretending to be a bigger sender than you are, because the truth arrives eventually, and when it does, the man who lied isn't embarrassed, he's gone. I don't punish honesty, ever, even when the honest answer is “I'm broke this month” or “I'm not comfortable with that” or “I don't know what I'm doing.” Honest men get taken care of. Liars get remembered, and not in the way anyone wants to be remembered.</p>
        <p>And honesty means honesty with yourself. If what you actually want is to be drained, say so. If what you actually want is to be kept, say so. If you don't know yet, say that. “I don't know yet, Goddess” is a perfectly respectable answer. It's the beginning of every good dynamic I've ever run.</p>
        <hr class="ways-divider">
        <h2>What It Means to Be <em>My Sub.</em></h2>
        <p>The rules above tell you how to behave. This tells you what you're signing up to be. Read it before you fill out the intake, because filling out the intake means you've read it and agreed.</p>
        <p>You are not a customer. Customers buy a product and leave. You are applying to belong to a woman, and belonging is different in every way that counts. It's ongoing. It's personal. It's remembered. I learn my Subs. I remember your details, your deadlines, your anniversaries, your fears. Customers don't get remembered. Mine do.</p>
        <p>You are led. I set the rhythm, the pace, the direction, and the standards. You don't steer. You don't negotiate the dynamic after it's established. You don't get to decide when you've been good, because that's my job, and I'm better at it than you. You follow instructions, you complete tasks, you report back honestly, and you trust that where I'm leading you is somewhere good, because I have never once led a good man somewhere bad.</p>
        <p>You are seen. This is the part nobody expects and everybody stays for. Being my Sub means being known. I pay attention. I ask questions. I remember. And somewhere down the road, you'll realize that this woman knows things about you that no one else in your life knows, and that she's never once used them against you, and that being known like that, completely and safely, is the thing you didn't know you were starving for.</p>
        <p>You are safe. Limits are respected, always. Discretion matters deeply to me, and I handle private information carefully. Read my <a href="/privacy.php">Discretion &amp; Privacy</a> page for a clear account of the protections currently in place.</p>
        <p>You are held to a standard. I'm a gentle goddess, and I want to be clear that gentle doesn't mean soft. I lead with warmth, I praise generously, and I expect a great deal. My men rise to my standards because my standards are worth rising to. And when you fall short, and you will, you'll get the quiet, the four words, the withdrawal. You already know how that works. Good men work very hard to avoid it, and are better men for the effort.</p>
        <p>You give, and you're given to. This is a dynamic, not a drain (unless draining is what you've asked for, and some of my men have). You give your tribute, your effort, your honesty, and in return you get my attention, my structure, my memory, my warmth, and a place in the world of a woman who is building something extraordinary. Nobody in my world gives into a void. Even my drained ones are seen while they're emptied. Even my set-apart ones are Mine.</p>
        <p>And you may, if it's yours, belong as family. Some of my men serve me as a Daddy serves his Little. Yes, the caretaking runs toward me, and if that sentence made something in your chest go quiet and attentive, the intake has questions for you.</p>
        <p>That's what it means to be Mine.</p>
        <p>Three rules. Clear as glass. A role with weight and warmth in it. And somewhere in my world, a place that might be waiting for you, if you're very good.</p>
